#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:1
msgid "Kernel Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:3
msgid ""
"This section documents kernel command-line parameters supported by Asterinas."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:5
msgid "Inherited from Linux"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:7
msgid "`init`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:9
msgid "Run the specified binary as `init`."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:11
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:67
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:100
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:16
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:48
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:72
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:106
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:17
msgid "The value is the path to the executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:18
msgid ""
"If omitted, Asterinas will try to execute from the following paths in order: "
"`/sbin/init`, `/etc/init`, `/bin/init`, `/bin/sh`."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:21
msgid "`console`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:23
msgid ""
"Select console devices for kernel messages. This parameter may be specified "
"multiple times. Kernel messages are delivered to each listed console."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:27
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:118
msgid "Valid values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:28
msgid "`tty0`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:29
msgid "`ttyS0`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:30
msgid "`hvc0`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:32
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:54
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:122
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:38
msgid "`virtio_mmio.device`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:40
msgid ""
"Register a VirtIO-MMIO device from the kernel command line. This parameter "
"may be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:43
msgid "Format:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:49
msgid "`size` and `base` may be decimal or hexadecimal with a `0x` prefix."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:50
msgid "`size` may use `K`, `M`, `G`, or `T` suffixes."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:51
msgid "`irq` must be nonzero."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:52
msgid ""
"The optional `id` field is accepted for Linux compatibility but ignored."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:60
#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:112
msgid "Asterinas-specific"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:61
msgid "`earlycon`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:63
msgid ""
"Enable the early console to output logs during the early stages of system "
"boot. The name follows Linux's `earlycon` parameter. Asterinas currently "
"supports a simplified form."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:73
msgid "If omitted, the early console stays disabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:74
msgid ""
"Only the bare `earlycon` token is supported; complex Linux forms such as "
"`earlycon=uart8250,io,0x3f8,115200` are not supported yet."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:77
msgid "`loglevel`"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:79
msgid ""
"Control how verbose kernel log output is on the console. Set either a "
"numeric value (`0` to `8`) or a lowercase level name."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:82
msgid ""
"Each value acts as a cutoff: messages at that severity and all more urgent "
"levels are printed. For example, `loglevel=4` shows emergencies through "
"errors, but not warnings or routine info."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/linux-compatibility/kernel-parameters.md:85
msgid ""
"This uses the same `0`–`8` scale as the Linux kernel `loglevel` parameter, "
"with string aliases for convenience."
msgstr ""

